<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Misl</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Misls, Bhangi Misl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A misl was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-confederacy">Sikh confederacies</a> that controlled parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in the eighteenth century, each led by a chief. Among them were the Sukerchakia and Bhangi misls. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukerchakia-misl">Sukerchakia misl</a>, united the misls under his rule, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/misl.jpg" alt="Misl" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Borders by Rawn3012 using Gimp · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Sikh_Confederacy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
